[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2653984235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102767#issuecomment-2653984235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102767","id":2653984235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eMJXr","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-12T15:04:35Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T15:25:26Z","body":"Sounds very similar to my proposal - [New pathfinding method for huge worlds](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9800)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2653984235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2656303382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102767#issuecomment-2656303382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102767","id":2656303382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eU_kW","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T11:25:45Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T11:25:45Z","body":"> Maybe I'm not reading this correctly, but it seems like the path and radius limits are only here to clamp the result at the end. We could instead use this to limit iterations during the search path, because it seems like if we have a huge navmesh, this won't help on the performance side, as the whole map will be searched, and then we clamp. We should use it to limit the A* search.\r\n\r\nIt is mostly a postprocessing yes, not a performance optimization. We don't have a hierarchical structure yet that we could use so we would at least need to work with a very big margin to the search.\r\n\r\nThe problem what else ends up happening when you just stop the path search after the limit is that you will get nonsensical paths all the time with no direction stability should the path update. The paths will commonly go into the completely wrong direction as soon as any navmesh layout is even slighty more complex, and that is unwanted. E.g. Detour pathfinding with cap suffers greatly from this with the search and the only saving grace that it has is the tilemesh as the tilemesh hierarchical connections allows it to at least somehow head into a reasonable direction, and we dont have something similar yet.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2656303382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896052391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102767#issuecomment-2896052391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102767","id":2896052391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6snkCn","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-20T23:27:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T23:27:00Z","body":"> When so. uses max length or max radius, an agent can stop in the middle of a navigation link\r\n\r\nNavigation links are all supposed to be script handled that facilitate the agent movement through a link. Outside of the most naive cases links do not function without a script as any map or path update would make it go back to the closest real navmesh polygon.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896052391/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970502868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102767#issuecomment-2970502868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102767","id":2970502868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xDkbU","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T13:58:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T13:58:53Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970502868/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"p